-- title:
--   Switcheroo Aggregate Left Front Scalar Close First Split Scalar
-- statement:
--   **The left-front scalar is within the commutation square root of the first-split scalar.**
--
--   Let `psi_bi` be normalized and suppose the left and right switcheroo point-product families satisfy an `SDDOpRel` bound with error `chi` over uniform slice-pair questions. If $S_{\mathrm{front}}$ is the left-front aggregate scalar and $S_{\mathrm{split}}$ is the first-split scalar, then
--
--   $$
--   \left|S_{\mathrm{front}}-S_{\mathrm{split}}\right|\le\sqrt{\chi}.
--   $$
--
--   The contraction estimate and the two point-product normalization identities reduce the final fourth-term comparison to this single square-root loss. The split scalar is then identified with the positive switcheroo term by later lemmas.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooAggregateLeftFrontScalar_close_firstSplitScalar`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
